{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3nfYTDxVnW8Yaqrxby1","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed \"wholsale\" to \"wholesale\" in all three files. The commit, `a143fd0`, only contains October and November, because the December file isn't tracked by git. `scripts/check.sh` printed `OK` before I committed.\n\n- **In the commit:** `data/2025-10.csv` and `data/2025-11.csv`, one line each. You can revert both in one go.\n- **Not in the commit:** December has still only been fixed in `inbox/2025-12.csv`, since it was never added to `data/`. git doesn't track `inbox/`, so reverting `a143fd0` won't undo that edit, and I can't revert it for you later. If you add December to `data/` from the inbox, it will bring the corrected spelling with it.\n\nThe project's rule is that commit messages start with the data month, but this change covers two months. I used \"2025-10, 2025-11:\" as the prefix. If the import log needs a single month, I can reword the commit.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":305,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":278,"cache_read_input_tokens":19168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":278,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-52>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:44:25.509Z","request_id":"gen-1794703461-zFQzQOvfl8L8tGOARvFm"}
